# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# askPESU -- local development environment
#
# Copy this file to `.env` at the repository root and fill in the blanks:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# One root .env serves BOTH services. python-dotenv's load_dotenv() searches
# upwards from the module that calls it, so running services/api or services/db
# from anywhere inside the repo picks this file up. `.env` is gitignored and
# must never be committed.
#
# In production nothing reads this file: Hugging Face Spaces inject the same
# names as environment variables from each Space's Settings -> Secrets.
#
# Write values UNQUOTED. python-dotenv strips surrounding quotes, but
# `docker run --env-file .env` -- the command the README documents -- does not:
# it passes the quote characters through as part of the value, so a quoted URL
# or key reaches the container malformed and the service fails to connect.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Qdrant -- services/api reads the collection, services/db writes it

# Cluster URL, e.g. https://xxxxxxxx-xxxx.europe-west3-0.gcp.cloud.qdrant.io:6333
# Qdrant Cloud -> your cluster -> Overview -> Endpoint (API keys are alongside it)
QDRANT_URL=
QDRANT_API_KEY=

# Which collection in that cluster. Required, with no default: defaulting would
# let a misconfigured deployment quietly read or write the wrong data.
#
# The deployed services all share ONE collection, ask-pesu-prod -- one db Space
# writes it, both api Spaces read it. Locally, use ask-pesu-dev instead, so that
# running the listener on your machine cannot touch the live index.
#
# Both services must be given the SAME value. Each verifies the shape of whatever
# it is pointed at, but neither can tell that the other was pointed elsewhere.
#
# The API key must be scoped to this collection: a Qdrant JWT scoped to a
# different name returns 403, and a scoped key's collection listing shows only
# what it grants, so it cannot be used to check what exists.
QDRANT_COLLECTION=

# --- Hugging Face -- services/api only

# Required. services/api raises KeyError at startup without it. It authenticates
# the Inference calls to the Qwen models AND the download of the embedding and
# reranker models.
# Create at https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens -- a "Read" token is enough,
# unless you also intend to push to the Spaces, which needs "Write".
HF_TOKEN=

# --- Reddit -- services/db only

# A "script"-type app: https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps -> create another app.
# REDDIT_CLIENT_ID is the string under the app name; REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET is the
# field labelled "secret".
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Optional

# Set to "test" to make services/api stream a canned response from /ask instead
# of calling the LLM. Useful for frontend work without burning inference quota.
# ENV=test
